#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# complex_plot

#% text
# `complex_plot(f, [z, z0, z1])` shows f over the rectangle of the complex plane with corners z0 and z1 by domain colouring.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The hue is the argument of f (red for positive reals, then yellow, green, cyan, blue, magenta going round); the colour is dark near zeros and light near poles.

#% item
# f is evaluated at 120 by 120 points.

#% item
# The value is `image("path")`, a PNG with SVG and PDF copies next to it.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Two zeros:

#% cell
complex_plot(z^2 - 1, [z, -2 - 2im, 2 + 2im])
#% output
#= image("complex_plot.files/complex_plot-1.png")

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A pole and a zero:

#% cell
complex_plot((z - 1)/(z + 1), [z, -2 - 2im, 2 + 2im])
#% output
#= image("complex_plot.files/complex_plot-2.png")

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The zeros of a polynomial:

#% cell
complex_plot(z^5 - 1, [z, -1.5 - 1.5im, 1.5 + 1.5im])
#% output
#= image("complex_plot.files/complex_plot-3.png")

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `complex_plot3d`, `re_im_plot`, `abs_arg_plot`, `density_plot`
